CRITERION 1 -- the wiring, not just the helper. PASS, with one dimension that
no command can demonstrate at the MCP boundary (stated explicitly below).

Command (scratch copy of the verified tree):
  TZ=America/New_York go test -count=1 ./internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/ -run TestZZ_C1 -v
  TZ=Asia/Tokyo       go test -count=1 ./internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/ -run TestZZ_C1 -v
Test: zzchecker_test.go TestZZ_C1_BranchWiringThroughTool -- a real MCP round trip
(connect() -> mcp client -> get_balance_projection) over one fixture with inbound
paired transfers at now-60 (100.00), now-30 (200.00) and now+10 (900.00). Truncation
is observable through reference_amount because medianInboundPairedTransfer
(projection.go:249-265) applies no date filter of its own.

  TZ=America/New_York as_of absent          -> as_of="2026-08-19" reference_amount=200.00
  TZ=America/New_York as_of empty string    -> as_of="2026-08-19" reference_amount=200.00
  TZ=America/New_York as_of whitespace only -> as_of="2026-08-19" reference_amount=200.00
  TZ=America/New_York as_of explicit today  -> as_of="2026-08-19" reference_amount=150.00
  TZ=Asia/Tokyo       as_of absent          -> as_of="2026-08-20" reference_amount=200.00
  TZ=Asia/Tokyo       as_of empty string    -> as_of="2026-08-20" reference_amount=200.00
  TZ=Asia/Tokyo       as_of whitespace only -> as_of="2026-08-20" reference_amount=200.00
  TZ=Asia/Tokyo       as_of explicit today  -> as_of="2026-08-20" reference_amount=150.00

So, through the real tool: absent / "" / "   " all take the NO-TRUNCATION branch;
an explicit date takes the TRUNCATED branch (the future 900.00 leg disappears).
asOfSupplied is derived at accounts.go:212-220 from `strings.TrimSpace(in.AsOf) != ""`
inside the same guard that decides whether to parse, so the three "no value" forms
cannot diverge from each other; the table above confirms that empirically, and the
as_of echo is today in all three.

Explicit as_of takes the DetectRecurringAt path, at integration:
  zzchecker_test.go:97  TZ=... historical as_of=2026-04-01 -> crossing="2026-05-01" minimum=100.00 topup=400.00
  zzchecker_test.go:113 control (DetectRecurring MaxDate fallback, untruncated) -> crossing=zero minimum=1000.00
(the control is the pre-R5 formula computed over the same deps.load() set, so the
fixture genuinely discriminates the two reference dates).

STATED LIMIT: whether the DEFAULT branch calls DetectRecurring rather than
DetectRecurringAt(now) CANNOT be observed through get_balance_projection's output
fields. Proven, not assumed: under mutation (a) below the tool's response is
byte-identical
  tool={AccountID:checking Available:true AsOf:2026-08-19 Threshold:500 Crossing: Minimum:1300 SuggestedTopUp:0 ReferenceAmount:0 HasReference:false}
while the recurring input changes from 1 payment to 0. Cause is R12 (excluded from
this task): Project's byDay map (projection.go:113-137) keys time.Time values built
from tx.Date (UTC) and looks them up with keys built from dayOf(asOf) (Local when
asOf==time.Now()); time.Time equality includes the *Location pointer, so no
occurrence is ever applied on the default path. The wiring is nonetheless
established: accounts.go:292-310 is a single `if !asOfSupplied` whose one boolean
selects BOTH the truncation and the recurring call, the handler's only call site is
accounts.go:235 and it passes the returned slice straight to accounts.Project at
:241, and the table above proves at integration which branch the tool executes.

