TEST-HONESTY REVIEW (committed tests read, not just their names)

- TestGetBalanceProjectionDefaultAsOfDoesNotTruncateReferenceAmount
  (accounts_test.go:641): fixture really does contain a future-dated (now+10)
  inbound paired transfer with a matching -900.00 leg in schwab.csv, and asserts
  reference_amount == 200.00. Non-vacuous: mutation (b) makes it fail with 150.00.
- TestGetBalanceProjectionDefaultAsOfReferenceAmountStableAcrossTimezones
  (accounts_test.go:701): tomorrow-edge (now+1) leg, asserts 200.00 and prints
  time.Local. Non-vacuous under Asia/Tokyo (mutation (b) -> 150.00); it does NOT
  discriminate under America/New_York, which is a property of the bug, not a defect
  in the test -- the doc comment says so and instructs running two zones.
- TestActiveSetAndRecurringForProjectionDefaultMeasuresFreshnessAgainstLedgerMaxDate
  (accounts_test.go:769): calls the real branch point with asOfSupplied=false,
  asserts exactly 1 detected series named "rent", AND contains a setup check that
  insights.DetectRecurringAt(ts, now) returns 0 on the same fixture -- so the
  fixture is proven to discriminate the two reference dates rather than assumed to.
  It is a unit test of the wiring decision, not of a downstream helper.
- TestGetBalanceProjectionDefaultAsOfUnchanged (accounts_test.go:547) is still the
  weak pin attempt 1 was failed for (no transfers, no 3+-occurrence merchant); it is
  now supplemented, not relied on. Its own comment admits the limitation.
- TestGetBalanceProjectionHistoricalAsOf... / ...FutureAsOf... assert the same
  values as attempt 1 and both fail under a one-day boundary shift or under the
  MaxDate-fallback control, so they still mean what their names claim.

